winemac: Implement cross-process child window Metal swapchains.

Upstream handles the top level case but declines a child window with a FIXME,
so a client whose GPU process renders into a child HWND owned by another
process gets nothing on screen.  Steam's chromium GPU process does exactly
that, which leaves the whole client UI black.

CALayerHost takes its size from the remote layer tree and ignores whatever
frame the hosting side sets, so the child's offset has to be baked in by the
sender: the drawable is wrapped in a container layer the size of the top
level's client area and positioned at the child's offset within it, with
geometryFlipped so the tree stays in windows coordinates.

A child window has no Cocoa window of its own, so the receiving side hosts the
layer on a view created for the purpose (macdrv_win_data.ca_host_view) rather
than on a window's content view, and disposes of it with the window.

